## SQ-TD-01 | reset
@group server
@commands `/ccaltime date`; `/ccaltime date add 40 days`; `/ccaltime date reset`; `/ccaltime date`; `/time query daytime`; `/season`
@pass after reset "Year 1, Early Spring, day 1 of 8, 7:42 am (world day 1)", daytime 0, `/season` Early Spring day 1
@fails start() or firstSunrise offset wrong
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb passed
> cetime date
# units are singular (day, month, season, year): `40 days` is refused (TI-32 and the queue wrote days)
> cetime date add 40 day
> cetime date reset
> cetime date
> time query daytime
expect Year 1, Early Spring, day 1 of 8, 7:42 am \(world day 1\)
expect The time is [0-9]{1,2}$
expect (?i)early spring

## SQ-TD-02 | next / previous / restart
@group server
@commands `/ccaltime date next month` x3, `/ccaltime date` after each; `/ccaltime date previous season`; `/ccaltime date add 3 days`; `/ccaltime date restart month`
@pass Mid Spring, Late Spring, Early Summer day 1 6:00 am; then Early Spring day 1; then Early Spring day 4 -> day 1
@fails unit alignment or now() wrong
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
> cetime date next month
> cetime date
> cetime date next month
> cetime date
> cetime date next month
> cetime date
> cetime date previous season
> cetime date
> cetime date add 3 day
> cetime date
> cetime date restart month
> cetime date
expect Mid Spring
expect Late Spring
expect Early Summer, day 1 of 8, 6:00 am
expect Early Spring, day 4
look order of the /cetime date answers: Mid Spring, Late Spring, Early Summer day 1 6:00 am, Early Spring day 1, Early Spring day 4, Early Spring day 1

## SQ-TD-03 | set an exact date, no double step
@group server
@commands `/ccaltime date set 3 mid_autumn 5 7:30 pm`; `/ccaltime date`; `/season`; wait 30 s; `/ccaltime date` again
@pass "Year 3, Mid Autumn, day 5 of 8, 7:30 pm (world day 253)"; `/season` agrees; 30 s later still day 5 (no double step)
@fails SeasonClock.jumped not reached, season counter added the jump twice
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb passed
> cetime date set 3 mid_autumn 5 7:30 pm
> cetime date
> season
sleep 30
> cetime date
expect Year 3, Mid Autumn, day 5 of 8, 7:30 pm \(world day 253\)
count Mid Autumn, day 5 >= 2
expect (?i)mid autumn

## SQ-TD-04 | wine clock follows
@group server
@commands `/wine clock set 0 days`; `/ccaltime date add 1 month`; `/wine time`; `/ccaltime date add -1 month`; `/wine time`
@pass clock 8 days after the forward step, back to about 0 after the backward one; chat says "wine clock moved back"; no WARN in latest.log
@fails VintageClock.add reflection failed (name or signature changed)
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
> wine clock set 0 days
> cetime date add 1 month
> wine time
> cetime date add -1 month
> wine time
reject (?i)WARN.*(VintageClock|wine)
look wine time reads 8 days after the forward step and about 0 after the backward one; the chat line "wine clock moved back" goes to the console too

## SQ-TD-05 | every /cetime date change is logged
@group server
@commands grep latest.log for `[time] /ccaltime date`
@pass one line per command with before / after position, dayTime and seasonCycleTicks
@fails logging missing
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
shell test "$(grep -c "\[time\] /cetime date" logs/latest.log)" -ge 8

## CQ-TD-06 | calendar on the client after a date set
@group client
@commands after SQ-TD-03 on a client: SeasonHUD line, calendar tooltip, Xaero time line
@pass "Autumn, Day 13/24 7:30 pm" (the pack HUD has `enable_show_sub_season = false`; corrected 2026-11-02), calendar Year 3, Xaero "Day 253, 19:30"; the world re-tints once
@fails client counter ran ahead (packet order)
@from batches/r1101/c1_client.qb
> cetime date set 3 mid_autumn 5 7:30 pm
sleep 5
shot hud
look SeasonHUD "Mid Autumn (Day 13/24) 7:30 pm", Xaero time line "Day 253, 19:30", the world re-tints once. hand: calendar item tooltip Year 3
> cetime date reset
